## Who is a two-week cure suitable for

A two-week stay is most often chosen by self-paying guests with chronic complaints of the musculoskeletal, circulatory or respiratory system, and by people who want to focus the stay on regeneration. Whether it is suitable for you, and with which programme, is assessed by the spa physician at the initial examination; the general contraindications to spa care (acute infections, decompensated heart failure, recent thrombosis and others) can be found in the [indication list](/en/indications-and-contraindications).

There are also randomised trials of two-week programmes, always for one specific diagnosis:

**Knee osteoarthritis:** In an Italian trial with 80 patients, a two-week cycle of peloid packs and baths improved pain and function and reduced the use of painkillers, for a period of 9 months; the control group did not change ([Fioravanti et al., 2010](https://consensus.app/papers/details/117ceeafb8b45fcb8ed8113fbdbc701c/), *Am J Phys Med Rehabil*). A systematic review reports that in knee osteoarthritis the effect of spa treatment is clinically meaningful for 3–6 months, sometimes up to 9 ([Forestier et al., 2016](https://consensus.app/papers/details/163b339826a2536eb7f05ce9b9111754/), *Ann Phys Rehabil Med*).

**Chronic low back pain:** In a Turkish trial with 60 patients, two-week balneotherapy improved pain and function still at 3 and 6 months; adding exercise made no further difference ([Takinaci et al., 2019](https://consensus.app/papers/details/08504c1e2ef354679262cc9364550b10/), *Eur J Integr Med*). Small sample.

**Rheumatoid arthritis:** In a crossover trial with 50 patients on disease-modifying drugs, adding two weeks of spa treatment improved disease activity and the global assessments of both patient and physician for up to 6 months ([Karagülle et al., 2018](https://consensus.app/papers/details/3a546f1db0215be397a42844e0a18000/), *Int J Biometeorol*). Drug treatment is led by the rheumatologist; the spa complements it.

**Blood pressure:** In a small study without a control group (35 patients), 24-hour blood pressure fell after three weeks of CO₂ baths and peloids in people with higher baseline values, and did not change in people with low pressure ([Ekmekcioglu et al., 2000](https://consensus.app/papers/details/39ccd0edaff45a03b6103309fbe833bc/), *Altern Ther Health Med*). In a randomised trial with 70 women with climacteric complaints, ten dry CO₂ baths reduced mean systolic pressure by 13.7% ([Chekhoeva et al., 2024](https://consensus.app/papers/details/e4851982210856378938913590dccac8/), *Bull Rehabil Med*). These are small studies; treatment of hypertension is led by your doctor, and a spa stay does not replace it.

The results of each of these trials apply to the given diagnosis and the given programme, not to every two-week stay.

## How much does a two-week cure cost?

**Accommodation with half board (14 nights):** €1,000–1,800 per person in a double room, depending on the hotel and season. The Ensana hotels offer the best combination of location, treatment infrastructure and value for money. Details on the [Accommodation](/en/accommodation) page.

**Treatment package:** €400–800 for a complete programme.

**Meals (beyond half board):** €150–280 for lunches and other expenses.

**Total budget per person:** €1,550–2,880. For couples in a double room, correspondingly cheaper per person.

## What to bring for 2 weeks

- Comfortable daywear (5–7 sets, laundry service at the hotel)
- Swimwear (2 sets)
- Sturdy shoes for forest paths
- Smart clothing for dinner
- A list of medications and current medical reports
- A bottle for spring water
- Reading for quiet evenings

## When is the best time?

**Spring (April–May):** Mild weather, blossoming parks, calm. Ideal for a first cure.

**Autumn (September–October):** Golden forests, mushrooms, fewer guests, lower prices. The favourite season of regular guests.

**Winter (November–February):** The lowest prices, maximum calm. The contrast of hot baths and frosty air has a charm of its own.

Book six to eight weeks ahead. Ensana offers [14-day spa packages](https://ensanahotels.com/en/offers) that bundle all services. Further information on getting there and local practicalities on the [Practical information](/en/practical-info) page.

Two weeks in Marienbad is not a break — it is two weeks devoted to yourself under the supervision of a physician. What you take home depends on your diagnosis: for knee osteoarthritis and chronic back pain, studies of two-week programmes suggest relief lasts 6 to 9 months. Many guests return every year; whether and when to return is recommended by the spa physician in the final report.
